#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[Notation]

Given a 1-type $X$, denote by $|"Aut"_X (-)| : X -> NN$ the set cardinality of the set of automorphisms.
The universal property of the set truncation gives a unique map from $||X||_0$ to $NN$, that is compatible with the Automorphism-Cardinality.
By abuse of notation we also denote this map by $|"Aut"_X (-)| : ||X||_0 -> NN$.
